      "prompt": "Dated source excerpts. Differences may reflect scope or conditions, not a resolved contradiction.\n[S1] NPS Ten Essentials\nDate: 2026-05-28 page updated; retrieved 2026-09-30\nSource: https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/articles\/10essentials.htm\nNAVIGATION – Map, compass, and GPS system Navigation items are used when planning your route before your trip, and when orienting yourself in the park during your activity. Know how to use a topographical map, compass or GPS unit before going out. Bring a physical map as a back up. You can also use the NPS app or download a map onto your phone or GPS. Pack an extra battery for your phone.\n\n[S2] Declaration of Independence (1776 historical text)\nDate: 1776-07-04 original document; retrieved 2026-09-30\nSource: https:\/\/www.archives.gov\/founding-docs\/declaration-transcript\nHe has excited domestic insurrections amongst us, and has endeavoured to bring on the inhabitants of our frontiers, the merciless Indian Savages, whose known rule of warfare, is an undistinguished destruction of all ages, sexes and conditions.\n\nQuestion: What navigation backups should I bring?\nUse one or two lines, adding a second only for supported detail.\nStart each line with source labels and then one factual sentence. Answer:",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "essentials-73b0434df1921710",
          "text": "NAVIGATION – Map, compass, and GPS system Navigation items are used when planning your route before your trip, and when orienting yourself in the park during your activity. Know how to use a topographical map, compass or GPS unit before going out. Bring a physical map as a back up. You can also use the NPS app or download a map onto your phone or GPS. Pack an extra battery for your phone.",
          "url": "https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/articles\/10essentials.htm",
          "rights": "National Park Service; ten-category system credited to The Mountaineers, Mountaineering: The Freedom of the Hills, 8th edition (2010); NPS explanatory text only; Public domain in the United States; https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/aboutus\/disclaimer.htm"
